# Base URL of the Flask export backend (no trailing slash).
# Leave unset for local development — the app falls back to http://localhost:3001.
# In Vercel, set this to the deployed backend URL, e.g. https://quote-gen-be.vercel.app
VITE_API_BASE=

# U-series feature flags — comma-separated allow-list, read once at build
# time (src/lib/featureFlags.js). This variable is ADDED TO the development
# floor in that file; it does not replace it.
#
# In a PRODUCTION build (`npm run build`) this variable is the whole story:
# unset or empty means every U-series screen is hidden and unmounted.
#
# In a DEVELOPMENT build (`npm run dev`) the two U1 DESTINATIONS are already on
# via featureFlags.js DEV_DEFAULTS, so a clean checkout can never lose them
# (UA-7 safeguard, u1-users-access-authorization-packet.md §5):
#   u1_producing_plants   — the read-only Producing Plants screen  [dev default]
#   u1_customer_families  — the read-only Customer Families screen [dev default]
#                            (also requires the caller's own read_party_master
#                            capability; the flag alone does not grant it)
#
# Flags whose rollout is deliberately explicit must be named here (or in an
# untracked .env.local) to appear at all. Being named here is a rollout
# choice, NOT a statement that the slice is unfinished:
#   u1_batch_party_link   — Slice D's governed Client quick-create/select.
#                            Slice D and Slice E are technically closed and
#                            Product Owner validated for the limited U1
#                            master-backed interaction scope; they are kept
#                            localhost-only on purpose.
##   freight_authority_v2  — S8(a). The CDM-17 freight chain: explicit zero,
#                            unresolved-blocks, and governed vs temporary
#                            provenance. NOT a dev default: it is an ENGINE
#                            flag, not a destination, so the dev floor's rule
#                            (featureFlags.js note 3) excludes it. With it OFF
#                            the unchanged pre-S8 freight path runs, bit for
#                            bit, including the legacy treatment of zero.
#
# Flipping one needs a rebuild — there is no runtime toggle.
# Example: VITE_FEATURE_FLAGS=u1_batch_party_link
VITE_FEATURE_FLAGS=
